@startuml lockfree-arc-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-arc-lifecycle.puml — the Arc refcount lifecycle across one CAS
' attempt: load bumps the count (no use-after-free), the built tree is handed
' off by raw pointer, a losing CAS reclaims-and-drops the rejected Arc, and an
' unreferenced old version deallocates when its count hits 0.
' Source: §Memory Management → Arc Reference Counting of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' NOTE: this is the SUPERSEDED pre-Phase-A raw-pointer path; the current
' owned-Child overlay reclaims by plain Arc refcounting with NO into_raw/
' from_raw (see the Phase-A box at the top of the doc).
' Color key (house palette):
'   green  #C8E6C9  ordinary safe Arc refcounting (auto reclaim)
'   amber  #FFE0B2  the raw-pointer handoff (into_raw / from_raw)
'   grey   #ECEFF1  load / plumbing
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #37474F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #FBC02D

title Arc lifecycle across one CAS attempt  (pre-Phase-A raw-pointer path)

start

partition "1 · Load from AtomicNodePtr (grey)" #ECEFF1 {
  :**Arc::increment_strong_count**\nbump refcount BEFORE returning\n→ prevents use-after-free;
}

partition "2 · Build the new tree (amber = raw handoff)" #FFE0B2 {
  :Arc::new — allocate new node versions;
  :**Arc::into_raw** — store as a raw\npointer inside SwizzledPtr (u64);
}

if (CAS(root: old → new) result?) then (fail — root moved)
  partition "3 · Reclaim the rejected Arc (amber)" #FFE0B2 {
    :**Arc::from_raw** — take ownership back\nand drop it (else it would leak);
  }
else (win — published)
  :new version is now the live root;
endif

partition "4 · Old version unreachable (green)" #C8E6C9 {
  :**Arc refcount → 0** → automatic\ndeallocation of the superseded node;
}

stop

note right
  Phase A removed into_raw/from_raw:
  children are an owned Child::InMem(Arc),
  so steps 2–3 are ordinary Arc moves;
  step 4 is unchanged.
end note
@enduml
